wildos-desktop (0.1.4) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Fingerprint readers work: fprintd and its PAM module come with the
    desktop. With a finger enrolled, the lock screen unlocks with a touch,
    and the sign-in screen, sudo and administrator prompts take an empty
    password as "use my finger" (pam-configs/wildos-fingerprint and
    fingerprint-turn). A typed password goes through the usual checks
    untouched, so a broken reader never locks anyone out, and a locked
    account stays locked.
  * /etc/pam.d/kde-fingerprint without pam_kwallet5, which asked for a
    password nobody could type and held the unlock after a good touch.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:30:00 +0000

